id: rust.rc-vs-arc
kind: rust
title: Rc vs Arc vs Box
aliases: rc, reference counting
tags: ownership, fundamentals
questions:
  - why can you not send an Rc across threads?
invariant: Rc counts non-atomically so it is neither Send nor Sync; Arc pays an atomic per clone to be shareable.
answer_30s: Rc is single-threaded and cheap, Arc uses atomics to be sendable across threads, and Box is unique ownership with no counting.
when_to_use:
  - Rc for single-threaded graphs; Arc across tasks; Box for exactly one owner
avoid_when:
  - reaching for Arc when the value is not shared (Box is free)
failure_modes:
  - building a single-threaded structure with Arc and paying atomic traffic for nothing
  - trying to move an Rc into tokio::spawn (a compile error whose real cause is a design mistake)
related:
  - rust.arc
  - rust.send-sync
sources:
  - https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/rc/struct.Rc.html
